From 4848de94428fc042ba7b4c5a7d01297483040ec0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LLCOOLT <114613597+LLCOOLT@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 12:18:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] display: HUD transform, anisotropy and LOD bias,
 supersampling, post filters, VRR

GXSetProjectionTransform (GX_AURORA_SET_PROJECTION_TRANSFORM): clip-space x
and y of following draws to the main framebuffer scaled and offset, their
scissor boxes too: a HUD larger or smaller about a point.
AuroraSetTextureAnisotropy / AuroraSetTextureLodBias: a floor on every
mipmapped texture's anisotropy, a bias added to every texture's LOD.
aurora_set_supersample: the framebuffer a whole multiple larger, area-
downsampled at present. aurora_set_post_filter: CRT, paper grain or sharpen
in the present resample pass. aurora_set_vrr: Immediate present whatever
vsync says. All in include/aurora/display.h.
